# The two Secrets statefulset.yaml.example reads, by these names and keys. Every
# value is left empty here on purpose. Fill a copy kept outside any repository,
# create the Secrets from it, and delete the filled copy; or create the same
# names and keys with the secret path you already use (an external secret
# store, kubectl create secret generic --from-file). Never commit a filled copy,
# never paste a value into a ConfigMap or the operator configuration, and check
# the keys afterwards by name only (SETUP.md, "Checking that it is up").
#
# An empty value is not a missing key: the Pod starts and every call that needs
# the credential fails (an empty tracker key logs "issue discovery unavailable:
# tracker credential is unavailable" on every poll). The status container is
# the exception: it refuses to start when either of its values is empty.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: <consumer>-ticket-engine
  namespace: <namespace>
type: Opaque
stringData:
  # The model provider's API key, for every model call in the shipped example:
  # the routing decision at the entrance, the per-launch model selection, every
  # model role and the review command. With the example as shipped this is an
  # OpenRouter API key (openrouter.ai, Keys). Set a credit limit on the key
  # itself: the engine has no spending limit of its own. Leave it out only when
  # every model call goes through a gateway (GATEWAY_API_KEY below) and no
  # setting names MODEL_API_KEY any more, and then also delete the three lines
  # of statefulset.yaml.example that read it: a key the Pod reads and the
  # Secret lacks keeps the Pod from starting.
  MODEL_API_KEY: ""
  # The tracker account the engine acts as (SETUP.md, "Preparing the tracker"):
  # a separate account that is a member of the project, never a requester's.
  # On Backlog: that account's personal settings, API, register a key. Only the
  # engine reads it; roles get a short-lived key scoped to their one issue.
  TRACKER_API_KEY: ""
  # The delivery identity's token, for one repository and without permission
  # over its workflows (SETUP.md, "Preparing the delivery repository"). The
  # mirror fetches with it, the delivery pushes the ticket branch, opens and
  # merges the pull request with it, and the merged check reads the integration
  # branch with it. No model role ever receives it.
  DELIVERY_GITHUB_TOKEN: ""
  # Only with a gateway in front of the model provider (rewrite/README.md,
  # "Invoking through a gateway"): the gateway's key. Uncomment it here and the
  # matching entry in statefulset.yaml.example together.
  # GATEWAY_API_KEY: ""
---
# HTTP basic authentication for the read-only status page. Choose both values
# yourself; nothing else uses them. The page shows everything in the queue,
# including each request's text, diffs and every role's output, so treat the
# password like any other credential.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: <consumer>-ticket-engine-status
  namespace: <namespace>
type: Opaque
stringData:
  STATUS_USER: ""
  STATUS_PASSWORD: ""
